# Mouse reporting on, which is what vim turns on: the wheel is a mouse code
# like any other button, and the protocol has no count — so two lines are two
# reports.
out "\x1b[?1000h\x1b[?1006h"
wheel 0 2 3 1
wheel 0 -1 3 1
# Sideways is its own pair of buttons.
wheel 1 0 3 1
# And what was held goes into the code, the same as it does for a click.
wheel 0 1 3 1 shift
